      "notes": "Captions and native complete diagrams reviewed. Native38 confirms the complete seventeen-piece final board after Ne5: White Kg2/Ra1/Nb1/Bf2/a2/b2/c3/g3/h2 against Kg8/Rd1/Ne5/a7/b7/e2/g7/h7, White to move. Independent h3 allows all four legal e1 promotions. Only e1=N+ gives check against Kg2; Q/R/B promotion does not. In every selected comparison Bxe1/Rxe1 legally exchanges the promoted piece and bishop into the SAME complete fifteen-piece ending. These are independently supplied alternatives, not recovered source moves or a certified forced sequence. The knight check does not prevent the bishop from capturing on e1. The full outcomes for other White moves, every promotion alternative and the larger rook/knight/pawn conversion remain pending. The original friendly-game ending was unrecorded/unremembered; no continuation is invented as actual play. All prior drafts, source images/captions and review history remain preserved.",
